{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>El Shaddai.</b> An epithet, and its meaning is 'powerful.' So too 'like the voice of Shaddai' (Ezekiel 1:24), 'and Shaddai will be your fortress' (Job 22:25), for its meaning is like that of 'and set your dust as a fortress' (Job 22:24). And שַדָי is on the pattern of לַבִּי דַוַּי (Lamentations 1:22), and many explained it from the root שודד, which means overcoming and prevailing. And the reason this name is mentioned in this pericope is to instill fear in Abram so that he circumcise. And the correct view is that the revered and awesome Name is called in correspondence to it, and this is an epithet corresponding to the deed, for the world stands upon these two names, and one who understands the sod of the Name will believe:" "<b>And be whole</b> — that you not ask why the circumcision:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved the ambiguous closing יאמין as a verb ('will believe'), though the subject is unstated."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:51.082765821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}